COMMERCIAL S11 BACKUP ROOT-MODE DIAGNOSIS

Status: ROOT_CAUSE_CONFIRMED; NO_S11_RUNTIME_MUTATION
Observed safe code: S11_BACKUP_VERIFY_RED

The retry passed source preflight and created the complete root-private backup.
Provenance, SHA-256 verification and both Git bundle verifications were green.
The deployment stopped before repository switching, package installation,
migration or feature activation because the backup root mode was 2700 rather
than the controller's required 0700.

The parent backup directory is setgid. A newly created child inherited that
special bit. The existing recursive `chmod go-rwx` removed all group and other
permissions but intentionally did not clear setgid, leaving a private 2700
directory. The verifier correctly rejected the exact-mode mismatch.

Bounded correction:
- Keep the parent and server configuration unchanged.
- After recursively removing group/other access, explicitly set the new backup
  root to 0700 before owner/mode evidence and checksums are produced.
- Keep the verifier's exact root:root:700 contract unchanged.

Backup and rollback:
- The stopped-attempt backup remains immutable and root-private; it is not
  modified or reused.
- No rollback was required because the controller had not armed or begun runtime
  mutation.
- The next attempt uses a fresh timestamped backup path.
- Immutable freezes r1 and r2 are not moved; the reviewed successor is r3.

Validation contract:
- Focused and complete Control tests, syntax, JSON and secret scan must pass.
- PR CI and same-SHA Codex review must pass.
- A green canonical post-merge CI and exact annotated r3 freeze are required
  before retry.
